{
 "summary": "Swapped the two alternatives of the PRERELEASEIDENTIFIER token in internal/re.js so the non-numeric form (\\d*[a-zA-Z-][a-zA-Z0-9-]*) is tried before the numeric one. Both forms accept disjoint identifier languages, so anchored consumers (FULL/LOOSE/XRANGE and the check in classes/semver.js) accept exactly the same strings and backtrack to the same match, but the unanchored COERCEFULL/COERCERTLFULL regexes used by semver.coerce({includePrerelease:true}) ended at the numeric prefix (the '7' of '7f3c') because their terminus check only rejects digits, truncating prerelease identifiers that start with a digit. The alternatives now consume the whole identifier, so 2.3.1-nightly.7f3c and 2.3.1-nightly.4821.9e1d coerce intact while all-digit and letter-leading identifiers are unchanged."
}

