 "summary": "In Version.next_version (src/semver/version.py), the branch handling old-style no-dot prereleases (e.g. rc9) returned the bumped counter unconditionally, which can sort below the input because alphanumeric SemVer identifiers compare lexically (rc10 < rc9). It now returns that candidate only when it compares greater than the original; otherwise it keeps the no-dot form and advances the patch (7.1.0-rc9 -> 7.1.1-rc10, rc99 -> rc100, beta9 -> 7.1.1-beta10), while ordinary steps (rc4 -> rc5) and the dotted style (rc.9 -> rc.10) keep the patch, as does the reported spec. Also documented the rollover behavior with a docstring example."
}
